\newlabel{overview}{{1}{2}{An overview of our proposed IRCL method. Class-invariant shared representation ($z$) is learned by a conditional variational autoencoder. A specific module is used to capture discriminative representation. The two representations are jointly used for learning continually a sequence of tasks. Pseudo-samples of previous tasks ($\hat  {x}$) are replayed with real data ($x$) of the current task to preserve the previously learned knowledge.}{}{}}
